# World organisation finder

Home Assistant has no household equivalent of worldwide government offices, so use this variant only for a genuine multi-home setup. There it identifies each configured home and the service it offers, with no implied government relationship. This is a recorded limit of the pattern: multi-home discovery is not implemented. Scope, result count, empty states, focus and the no-JavaScript fallback follow the [shared finder behaviour](../finder.html#finder-shared-contract).

## When to use it

Adapt only the directory principle for a genuine multi-home setup: identify each configured home and its available service.

## Home Assistant boundary

This does not add multi-home discovery, federation or remote access. Do not publish private addresses, network details or credentials in a navigation catalogue.

